      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-87573",
      ":question/problem": "A computer science center organizes a machine learning course. The course is activated if there are at least $3$ participants, and it can be attended by at most $13$ participants. The price for each participant is $$200$. The cost of providing the course is $C(x) = 200x - 4x^{3} + 0.3x^{4}$, where $x$ is the number of participants. What is the maximum profit that the computer science center can make?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
